From 659f821b7cced5621fa798108183f95e6c63659c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: infra <infra@davhau.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:16:56 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ws): keep the socket and the composer across a quick app
 switch

onStop released an idle socket at once, so every trip to another app
cost a ws-ticket + upgrade + session.resume round trip on return, with
the composer disabled (enabled = isConnected) until it finished.

- WsTransport: an idle socket outlives the app leaving the foreground by
  BACKGROUND_IDLE_GRACE_MS (60 s) before it is released; lease releases
  and turn ends inside the grace no longer close it early.
- Returning with the socket gone (Android cuts a backgrounded app's
  network within seconds) dials at once instead of waiting out the
  reconnect backoff.
- ChatComposer: the text field stays editable while reconnecting; only
  Send waits for the connection.
---
